CatRenderer.swift and KeyMap.swift are copied without modification.
CatPhysics.swift adds an optional scripted idle-age override for PetNest sleep preferences.
Bridge.swift is the PetNest adapter: supplies physical input and a bitmap target,
isolates preferences from KuroCat, and does not run upstream input monitors or startup code.
The original keycap badges, key layout, paw physics, cursor movement and petting are retained.
Windows currently uses the separate simplified Qt renderer, not this native library.
FatCat's Windows system cursor pack and annoyed-petting extension are not included.
